  "human_edit_summary": "Task-stage evidence re-bind, no human edit to tasks.md. Attempt 6's binding recorded the raw bytes of a status-mixed plan (six Done, T-006 Implementation Complete) and its own contract predicted it would go stale on T-006's Done flip. That flip happened: the independent quality gate at ledger sequence 681 returned PASS on the eighth review attempt (run on the human's explicit direction, ruling (b) of 2026-08-11 on RT-20260811-002, the class fix evicting the repo-shared workflow snapshot from both sibling bundles) and recorded Status: Done for T-006 (reports/quality-gate/20260811T111350Z-epic-190-a2-capability-registry-T-006.md). The only change to tasks.md since attempt 6 is that one lifecycle line; both reviewers re-ran their full check sets on the current document (PASS/PASS, zero findings; reviewer B records one honest SKIP, BUGFIX-DIAGNOSTIC-PATH, no bugfix task in scope). Durability, measured: all seven tasks are now at the terminal Done state, so no further lifecycle flip exists for this feature; tasks_sha256 below records the raw bytes (bff14179...), which check-workflow-state accepts via its raw-hash path, and the Done-canonical form rereview_normalized_hash(tasks.md, 'Done') = 532f0d2cf02203f163829eee40b3bef07dd9ee2441a625f43686db0d03aa1505 is additionally accepted for any future re-derivation (the two differ only because the normalizer strips the '(sudo <timestamp>)' audit marks from approval lines). Unlike attempts 5 and 6, this binding can no longer be invalidated by a lifecycle transition -- only by a body edit, which must invalidate it by design. WFI-025 remains the systemic fix for the underlying matching rule.",
